# THE TUNING (v0.3, Setup 2 KNOB 4, par110): a pitch knob's detent is the grid's next step, up or down (Evan,
# 2026-10-30, after #61's glide-and-land: every detent moves the pitch, and the card shows the note it goes to).
# Drone I's pitch (par0, cents over MIDI 0; D3 5000); the host's spin turns its detents at once: a first turn, no
# speed-up
set 74 0
set 51 0
tap PLAY
wait 500
expect par110 0
expect par0 5000
# four detents: four semitones, at once (F#3)
spin K1 4
expect par0 5400
wait 900
expect par0 5400
# SEL fine-tunes, 1 cent a detent, and that stays: +3 over every semitone it steps to after
press SEL
spin K1 3
release SEL
expect par0 5403
spin K1 2
expect par0 5603
spin K1 -1
expect par0 5503
# the grid goes round both ways: quarter tones (1)
tap GLO
tap GLO
spin K4 -1
expect par110 10
spin K4 1
spin K4 1
expect par110 1
# ... a detent is a quarter tone, still +3
tap HOME
spin K1 1
expect par0 5553
# SEL back on the grid (-3: the offset 0 again)
press SEL
spin K1 -3
release SEL
expect par0 5550
# just intonation (5), from A: off its grid, the first detent down is the grid's next below (5518, A's 15/8 over
# A2), then 5384 5314 5202 (5/3, 8/5, 3/2)
tap GLO
spin K4 1
spin K4 1
spin K4 1
spin K4 1
expect par110 5
tap HOME
spin K1 -4
expect par0 5202
# 53-tone (4): 1200/53 = 22.6 cents a step, from A (900): 5202 is step 190 (4302 over A); two up, 192: 5247
tap GLO
spin K4 -1
expect par110 4
tap HOME
spin K1 2
expect par0 5247
# LMY (6): La Monte Young's Well-Tuned Piano, as Ableton's file places it (A 440 one of its notes): uneven steps,
# one each detent. E4+2 (6402, 3/2 over A3) up: 6429 (32/21), 6465 (14/9), 6669 (7/4); down again: 6465 6429 6402
tap GLO
spin K4 1
spin K4 1
expect par110 6
tap HOME
set 0 6402
spin K1 1
expect par0 6429
spin K1 1
expect par0 6465
spin K1 1
expect par0 6669
spin K1 -1
expect par0 6465
spin K1 -1
expect par0 6429
spin K1 -1
expect par0 6402
wait 900
expect par0 6402
# the harmonics (7): from 6402 (702 over A3, the 3rd harmonic) up: 841 (13th): 6541
tap GLO
spin K4 1
expect par110 7
tap HOME
spin K1 1
expect par0 6541
# the shrutis (8, Sa on C, A 440 their Dha+): 6541 (841 over A3) up: 884 (5/3 from A): 6584
tap GLO
spin K4 1
expect par110 8
tap HOME
spin K1 1
expect par0 6584
# Lou Harrison's (9, his National Steel guitar's, A 440 one of its notes): 6584 (5/3 over A3) up: 996 (16/9): 6696;
# down twice: 6584, 6465 (14/9)
tap GLO
spin K4 1
expect par110 9
tap HOME
spin K1 1
expect par0 6696
spin K1 -2
expect par0 6465
# Harry Partch's 43 (10), from A: 6465 (765 over A3, 14/9) up: 792, 814 (128/81, 8/5): 6514
tap GLO
spin K4 1
expect par110 10
tap HOME
spin K1 2
expect par0 6514
tap GLO
spin K4 1
expect par110 0
spin K4 -1
expect par110 10
spin K4 1
tap HOME
# Pitch link on (par45): drone II's knob turns the link offset (par46), a step of the grid's intervals: a fifth
# (700) up one: 800
set 45 1
set 46 700
spin K3 1
expect par46 800
